-- ccc29-xxviii-4-appeal-812.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART XXVII, "Appeal": sections 812 to 828 (the appeal court, who may appeal, notice,
-- interim release of the appellant, the recognizance of the prosecutor, fixing a date, procedure on appeal, trial de novo, costs and enforcement).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. The text is a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation
-- (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text. The conventions of ccc29-xxviii-0-peace-810.l4 apply unchanged.
-- Periods the text leaves to rules of court (the time to give notice of appeal, the fixing of a date for costs) are inputs, never numbers from memory.

§ `Section 812 -- Definition of appeal court`

-- 812(1) For the purposes of sections 813 to 828, appeal court means (a) in the Province of Ontario, the Superior Court of Justice sitting in the region, district or county or group of counties where the adjudication was made; (b) in Quebec, the Superior Court; (c) in Nova Scotia, British Columbia, Prince Edward Island and Newfoundland and Labrador, the Supreme Court; (d) in New Brunswick, Manitoba, Saskatchewan and Alberta, the Court of Queen's Bench; (e) to (g) [repealed]; (h) in Yukon and the Northwest Territories, a judge of the Supreme Court; and (i) in Nunavut, a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice.
-- src:17119 | Definition of appeal court
-- src:17120 | 812 (1) For the purposes of sections 813 to 828, appeal court means
-- src:17121 | (a) in the Province of Ontario, the Superior Court of Justice sitting in the region, district or county or group of counties where the adjudication was made;
-- src:17122 | (b) in the Province of Quebec, the Superior Court;
-- src:17123 | (c) in the Provinces of Nova Scotia, British Columbia, Prince Edward Island and Newfoundland and Labrador, the Supreme Court;
-- src:17124 | (d) in the Provinces of New Brunswick, Manitoba, Saskatchewan and Alberta, the Court of Queen’s Bench;
-- src:17125 | (e) [Repealed, 1992, c. 51, s. 43]
-- src:17126 | (f) [Repealed, 2015, c. 3, s. 56]
-- src:17127 | (g) [Repealed, 2026, c. 11, s. 45]
-- src:17128 | (h) in Yukon and the Northwest Territories, a judge of the Supreme Court; and
-- src:17129 | (i) in Nunavut, a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice.
