    WHEN `s 812(1) Ontario` THEN `s 812(1)(a) the Superior Court of Justice sitting in the region, district or county or group of counties where the adjudication was made`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Quebec` THEN `s 812(1)(b) the Superior Court`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Nova Scotia` THEN `s 812(1)(c) the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `s 812(1) British Columbia` THEN `s 812(1)(c) the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Prince Edward Island` THEN `s 812(1)(c) the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Newfoundland and Labrador` THEN `s 812(1)(c) the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `s 812(1) New Brunswick` THEN `s 812(1)(d) the Court of Queen's Bench`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Manitoba` THEN `s 812(1)(d) the Court of Queen's Bench`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Saskatchewan` THEN `s 812(1)(d) the Court of Queen's Bench`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Alberta` THEN `s 812(1)(d) the Court of Queen's Bench`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Yukon` THEN `s 812(1)(h) a judge of the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `s 812(1) the Northwest Territories` THEN `s 812(1)(h) a judge of the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Nunavut` THEN `s 812(1)(i) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice`

-- 812(2) A judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut is the appeal court for the purposes of sections 813 to 828 if the appeal is from a conviction, order, sentence or verdict of a summary conviction court consisting of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice.
-- src:17130 | When appeal court is Court of Appeal of Nunavut
-- src:17131 | (2) A judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut is the appeal court for the purposes of sections 813 to 828 if the appeal is from a conviction, order, sentence or verdict of a summary conviction court consisting of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice.
@ref Criminal Code s 812(2) (src:17130-17131)
GIVEN place IS A `s 812(1) province or territory`
      `the appeal is from a conviction, order, sentence or verdict of a summary conviction court consisting of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 812 appeal court`
`s 812(2) the appeal court once subsection (2) is applied` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is from a conviction, order, sentence or verdict of a summary conviction court consisting of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice`
    THEN `s 812(2) a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut`   -- the text's own words: "A judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut is the appeal court ... if the appeal is from"
    ELSE `s 812(1) the appeal court for sections 813 to 828` place

§ `Section 813 -- Appeal by defendant, informant or Attorney General`

-- 813 Except where otherwise provided by law, (a) the defendant in proceedings under this Part may appeal to the appeal court (i) from a conviction or order made against him, (ii) against a sentence passed on him, or (iii) against a verdict of unfit to stand trial or not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder; and (b) the informant, the Attorney General or his agent in proceedings under this Part may appeal to the appeal court (i) from an order that stays proceedings on an information or dismisses an information, (ii) against a sentence passed on a defendant, or (iii) against a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial, and the Attorney General of Canada or his agent has the same rights of appeal in proceedings instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government as the Attorney General of a province or his agent has under this paragraph.
-- src:17132 | Appeal by defendant, informant or Attorney General
-- src:17133 | 813 Except where otherwise provided by law,
-- src:17134 | (a) the defendant in proceedings under this Part may appeal to the appeal court
-- src:17135 | (i) from a conviction or order made against him,
-- src:17136 | (ii) against a sentence passed on him, or
-- src:17137 | (iii) against a verdict of unfit to stand trial or not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder; and
-- src:17138 | (b) the informant, the Attorney General or his agent in proceedings under this Part may appeal to the appeal court
-- src:17139 | (i) from an order that stays proceedings on an information or dismisses an information,
-- src:17140 | (ii) against a sentence passed on a defendant, or
-- src:17141 | (iii) against a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial,
-- src:17142 | and the Attorney General of Canada or his agent has the same rights of appeal in proceedings instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government as the Attorney General of a province or his agent has under this paragraph.
@ref Criminal Code s 813 to s 813(b)(iii) (src:17132-17142)
DECLARE `s 813 appellant` IS ONE OF
    `s 813 the defendant in proceedings under this Part`
    `s 813 the informant`
    `s 813 the Attorney General or the Attorney General's agent`
    `s 813 the Attorney General of Canada or the Attorney General of Canada's agent`
    `s 813 another person`

DECLARE `s 813 decision appealed` IS ONE OF
    `s 813 a conviction or order made against the defendant`
    `s 813 a sentence passed on the defendant`
    `s 813 a verdict of unfit to stand trial`
    `s 813 a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder`
    `s 813 an order that stays proceedings on an information`
    `s 813 an order that dismisses an information`
    `s 813 another decision`

@ref Criminal Code s 813 to s 813(b)(iii) (src:17132-17142)
-- @name-test: kept JUST FALSE, gate closed by the text: "Except where otherwise provided by law" is the text's own exception
GIVEN appellant IS A `s 813 appellant`
      decision IS A `s 813 decision appealed`
      `the law otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings were instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` MEANS
    IF `the law otherwise provides`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except where otherwise provided by law"
    ELSE CONSIDER appellant
         WHEN `s 813 the defendant in proceedings under this Part` THEN
             CONSIDER decision
             WHEN `s 813 a conviction or order made against the defendant` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `s 813 a sentence passed on the defendant` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `s 813 a verdict of unfit to stand trial` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `s 813 a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `s 813 an order that stays proceedings on an information` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) gives the defendant three grounds, and a stay is not among them
             WHEN `s 813 an order that dismisses an information` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) gives the defendant three grounds
             WHEN `s 813 another decision` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) gives the defendant three grounds
         WHEN `s 813 the informant` THEN `s 813 the prosecution side may appeal` decision
         WHEN `s 813 the Attorney General or the Attorney General's agent` THEN `s 813 the prosecution side may appeal` decision
         WHEN `s 813 the Attorney General of Canada or the Attorney General of Canada's agent` THEN
             IF `the proceedings were instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government`
             THEN `s 813 the prosecution side may appeal` decision
             ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in proceedings instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government"
         WHEN `s 813 another person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraphs (a) and (b) name the defendant, the informant, the Attorney General and the agent

@ref Criminal Code s 813(b) (src:17138)
-- @name-test: no JUST FALSE branch; named for a power, answers NOTHING outside the decisions the prosecution side may appeal (called by s 813)
GIVEN decision IS A `s 813 decision appealed`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 813 the prosecution side may appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER decision
    WHEN `s 813 an order that stays proceedings on an information` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 813 an order that dismisses an information` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 813 a sentence passed on the defendant` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 813 a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 813 a verdict of unfit to stand trial` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 813 a conviction or order made against the defendant` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) gives the informant and the Attorney General three grounds, and a conviction is not among them
    WHEN `s 813 another decision` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) gives three grounds

§ `Sections 814 and 815 -- Where the appeal is heard; notice of appeal`

-- 814 (1) In Manitoba and Alberta an appeal under 813 shall be heard at the sittings of the appeal court held nearest to the place where the cause arose; (2) in Saskatchewan, at the sittings at the judicial centre nearest to the place where the adjudication was made; (3) in British Columbia, at the sittings held nearest to the place where the adjudication was made; the judge of the appeal court may, on the application of one of the parties, appoint another place. (4) In Yukon, the Northwest Territories and Nunavut, the appeal shall be heard at the place where the cause arose or at the place nearest to it where a court is appointed to be held.
-- src:17143 | Manitoba and Alberta
-- src:17144 | 814 (1) In the Provinces of Manitoba and Alberta, an appeal under section 813 shall be heard at the sittings of the appeal court that is held nearest to the place where the cause of the proceedings arose, but the judge of the appeal court may, on the application of one of the parties, appoint another place for the hearing of the appeal.
-- src:17145 | Saskatchewan
-- src:17146 | (2) In the Province of Saskatchewan, an appeal under section 813 shall be heard at the sittings of the appeal court at the judicial centre nearest to the place where the adjudication was made, but the judge of the appeal court may, on the application of one of the parties, appoint another place for the hearing of the appeal.
-- src:17147 | British Columbia
-- src:17148 | (3) In the Province of British Columbia, an appeal under section 813 shall be heard at the sittings of the appeal court that is held nearest to the place where the adjudication was made, but the judge of the appeal court may, on the application of one of the parties, appoint another place for the hearing of the appeal.
-- src:17149 | Territories
-- src:17150 | (4) In Yukon, the Northwest Territories and Nunavut, an appeal under section 813 shall be heard at the place where the cause of the proceedings arose or at the place nearest to it where a court is appointed to be held.
@ref Criminal Code s 814(1) to s 814(4) (src:17143-17150)
DECLARE `s 814 place of hearing` IS ONE OF
    `s 814(1) the sittings of the appeal court held nearest to the place where the cause of the proceedings arose`
    `s 814(2) the sittings of the appeal court at the judicial centre nearest to the place where the adjudication was made`
    `s 814(3) the sittings of the appeal court held nearest to the place where the adjudication was made`
    `s 814(4) the place where the cause of the proceedings arose or the place nearest to it where a court is appointed to be held`

@ref Criminal Code s 814(1) to s 814(4) (src:17143-17150)
GIVEN place IS A `s 812(1) province or territory`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 814 place of hearing`
`s 814 the place at which the appeal under section 813 is required to be heard` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `s 812(1) Manitoba` THEN JUST `s 814(1) the sittings of the appeal court held nearest to the place where the cause of the proceedings arose`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Alberta` THEN JUST `s 814(1) the sittings of the appeal court held nearest to the place where the cause of the proceedings arose`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Saskatchewan` THEN JUST `s 814(2) the sittings of the appeal court at the judicial centre nearest to the place where the adjudication was made`
    WHEN `s 812(1) British Columbia` THEN JUST `s 814(3) the sittings of the appeal court held nearest to the place where the adjudication was made`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Yukon` THEN JUST `s 814(4) the place where the cause of the proceedings arose or the place nearest to it where a court is appointed to be held`
    WHEN `s 812(1) the Northwest Territories` THEN JUST `s 814(4) the place where the cause of the proceedings arose or the place nearest to it where a court is appointed to be held`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Nunavut` THEN JUST `s 814(4) the place where the cause of the proceedings arose or the place nearest to it where a court is appointed to be held`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Ontario` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): sections 814(1) to (4) name no rule for this place
    WHEN `s 812(1) Quebec` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): sections 814(1) to (4) name no rule for this place
    WHEN `s 812(1) Nova Scotia` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): sections 814(1) to (4) name no rule for this place
    WHEN `s 812(1) Prince Edward Island` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): sections 814(1) to (4) name no rule for this place
    WHEN `s 812(1) Newfoundland and Labrador` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): sections 814(1) to (4) name no rule for this place
    WHEN `s 812(1) New Brunswick` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): sections 814(1) to (4) name no rule for this place

