§ `Sections 816 to 820 -- Interim release of the appellant; recognizance; review; fixing a date; waiver`

-- 816(1) A person who was the defendant in proceedings before a summary conviction court and who is an appellant under section 813 shall, if they are in custody, remain in custody unless the appeal court at which the appeal is to be heard makes a release order referred to in section 515, the form of which may be adapted to suit the circumstances, which must include the condition that the person surrender themselves into custody in accordance with the order.
-- src:17157 | Release order — appellant
-- src:17158 | 816 (1) A person who was the defendant in proceedings before a summary conviction court and who is an appellant under section 813 shall, if they are in custody, remain in custody unless the appeal court at which the appeal is to be heard makes a release order referred to in section 515, the form of which may be adapted to suit the circumstances, which must include the condition that the person surrender themselves into custody in accordance with the order.
@ref Criminal Code s 816(1) (src:17157-17158)
GIVEN `the person was the defendant in proceedings before a summary conviction court and is an appellant under section 813` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal court at which the appeal is to be heard makes a release order referred to in section 515` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 816(1) the appellant is required to remain in custody` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person was the defendant in proceedings before a summary conviction court and is an appellant under section 813` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who was the defendant in proceedings before a summary conviction court and who is an appellant under section 813"
        IF NOT `the person is in custody` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if they are in custody"
        IF `the appeal court at which the appeal is to be heard makes a release order referred to in section 515` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the appeal court at which the appeal is to be heard makes a release order"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref Criminal Code s 816(1) (src:17157-17158)
GIVEN `the release order is one made by the appeal court under section 816(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 816(1) the release order is required to include the condition that the person surrender themselves into custody in accordance with the order` MEANS
    IF `the release order is one made by the appeal court under section 816(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a release order referred to in section 515 ... which must include the condition"

