-- 817(1) The prosecutor in proceedings before a summary conviction court by whom an appeal is taken under section 813 shall, immediately after filing the notice of appeal and proof of service of the notice in accordance with section 815, appear before a justice, and the justice shall, after giving the prosecutor and the respondent a reasonable opportunity to be heard, order that the prosecutor enter into a recognizance, with or without sureties, in the amount that the justice directs and with or without the deposit of money or other valuable security that the justice directs.
-- src:17163 | Recognizance of prosecutor
-- src:17164 | 817 (1) The prosecutor in proceedings before a summary conviction court by whom an appeal is taken under section 813 shall, immediately after filing the notice of appeal and proof of service of the notice in accordance with section 815, appear before a justice, and the justice shall, after giving the prosecutor and the respondent a reasonable opportunity to be heard, order that the prosecutor enter into a recognizance, with or without sureties, in the amount that the justice directs and with or without the deposit of money or other valuable security that the justice directs.
@ref Criminal Code s 817(1) (src:17163-17164)
GIVEN `the person is the prosecutor in proceedings before a summary conviction court by whom an appeal is taken under section 813` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor has filed the notice of appeal and proof of service of the notice in accordance with section 815` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is taken by the Attorney General or counsel acting on behalf of the Attorney General, by s 817(3) section 817 does not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 817(1) the prosecutor is required to appear before a justice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is the prosecutor in proceedings before a summary conviction court by whom an appeal is taken under section 813` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The prosecutor in proceedings before a summary conviction court by whom an appeal is taken under section 813"
        IF `the appeal is taken by the Attorney General or counsel acting on behalf of the Attorney General, by s 817(3) section 817 does not apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply in respect of an appeal taken by the Attorney General"
        IF NOT `the prosecutor has filed the notice of appeal and proof of service of the notice in accordance with section 815` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "immediately after filing the notice of appeal and proof of service of the notice"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref Criminal Code s 817(1) (src:17163-17164)
GIVEN `the prosecutor has appeared before the justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice has given the prosecutor and the respondent a reasonable opportunity to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 817(1) the justice is required to order that the prosecutor enter into a recognizance` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor has appeared before the justice` AND `the justice has given the prosecutor and the respondent a reasonable opportunity to be heard`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after giving the prosecutor and the respondent a reasonable opportunity to be heard"

DECLARE `s 817 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 817(1) appear before a justice`
    `s 817(1) order that the prosecutor enter into a recognizance`

@ref Criminal Code s 817(1) (src:17163-17164)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 817 action`
`s 817(1) the justice is to order that the prosecutor enter into a recognizance` MEANS
    PARTY `a justice`
    MUST `s 817(1) order that the prosecutor enter into a recognizance`

@ref Criminal Code s 817(1) (src:17163-17164)
-- "Immediately after filing" is WITHIN 0 days of the filing. The justice's duty follows the prosecutor's appearance and carries no time of its own.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 817 action`
`s 817(1) the prosecutor is to appear before a justice` MEANS
    PARTY `the prosecutor`
    MUST `s 817(1) appear before a justice`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE `s 817(1) the justice is to order that the prosecutor enter into a recognizance`
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the prosecutor did not appear before a justice immediately after filing the notice of appeal"

