-- 818(1) Where a justice makes an order under section 817, either the appellant or the respondent may, before or at any time during the hearing of the appeal, apply to the appeal court for a review of the order made by the justice.
-- src:17170 | Application to appeal court for review
-- src:17171 | 818 (1) Where a justice makes an order under section 817, either the appellant or the respondent may, before or at any time during the hearing of the appeal, apply to the appeal court for a review of the order made by the justice.
@ref Criminal Code s 818(1) (src:17170-17171)
-- @name-test: listed, where/when/upon kind (F-818-1): "Where a justice makes an order under section 817" and "before or at any time during the hearing" answer JUST FALSE
GIVEN `a justice makes an order under section 817` IS A BOOLEAN
