-- 819(1) Where, in the case of an appellant who has been convicted by a summary conviction court and who is in custody pending the hearing of his appeal, the hearing of his appeal has not commenced within thirty days from the day on which notice of his appeal was given in accordance with the rules referred to in section 815, the person having the custody of the appellant shall, forthwith on the expiration of those thirty days, apply to the appeal court to fix a date for the hearing of the appeal.
-- src:17178 | Application to fix date for hearing of appeal
-- src:17179 | 819 (1) Where, in the case of an appellant who has been convicted by a summary conviction court and who is in custody pending the hearing of his appeal, the hearing of his appeal has not commenced within thirty days from the day on which notice of his appeal was given in accordance with the rules referred to in section 815, the person having the custody of the appellant shall, forthwith on the expiration of those thirty days, apply to the appeal court to fix a date for the hearing of the appeal.
@ref Criminal Code s 819(1) (src:17178-17179)
-- Fork F-819-1: "within thirty days from the day on which notice was given" is counted from the day after that day: the thirty days expire on the notice day PLUS 30. The other reading counts the notice day as day 1.
GIVEN `the day on which notice of the appeal was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 819(1) the day on which the thirty days expire` MEANS
    `the day on which notice of the appeal was given` PLUS 30

@ref Criminal Code s 819(1) (src:17178-17179)
GIVEN `the appellant has been convicted by a summary conviction court and is in custody pending the hearing of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hearing of the appeal has commenced within thirty days from the day on which notice of the appeal was given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 819(1) the person having the custody of the appellant is required to apply to the appeal court to fix a date for the hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the appellant has been convicted by a summary conviction court and is in custody pending the hearing of the appeal` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, in the case of an appellant who has been convicted by a summary conviction court and who is in custody pending the hearing of his appeal"
        IF `the hearing of the appeal has commenced within thirty days from the day on which notice of the appeal was given` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the hearing of his appeal has not commenced within thirty days"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 819 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 819(1) apply to the appeal court to fix a date for the hearing of the appeal`
    `s 819(2) fix a date for the hearing of the appeal and give directions for expediting the hearing`

@ref Criminal Code s 819(1) (src:17178-17179)
-- "Forthwith on the expiration" is WITHIN 0 days of the expiry of the thirty days.
-- The person having the custody of the appellant is modelled as the keeper of a prison (assumed, not ruled: the text names no office).
