    IF NOT (`the day on which the appeal is to be heard` AT MOST `the day on which the material is transmitted`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the appeal court has directed a further time` AND `the day on which the material is transmitted` AT MOST `the further day directed by the appeal court`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the time when the appeal is to be heard, or within such further time as the appeal court may direct"

@ref Criminal Code s 821(1) (src:17188-17189)
