§ `Sections 825 to 828 -- Dismissal, costs and enforcement`

-- 825 The appeal court may, on proof that notice of an appeal has been given and that (a) the appellant has failed to comply with the conditions of a release order made under section 816 or of a recognizance entered into under section 817; or (b) the appeal has not been proceeded with or has been abandoned, order that the appeal be dismissed.
-- src:17227 | Dismissal for failure to appear or want of prosecution
-- src:17228 | 825 The appeal court may, on proof that notice of an appeal has been given and that
-- src:17229 | (a) the appellant has failed to comply with the conditions of a release order made under section 816 or of a recognizance entered into under section 817; or
-- src:17230 | (b) the appeal has not been proceeded with or has been abandoned,
-- src:17231 | order that the appeal be dismissed.
@ref Criminal Code s 825 to s 825(b) (src:17227-17231)
