GIVEN `there is proof that notice of the appeal has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant has failed to comply with the conditions of a release order made under section 816 or of a recognizance entered into under section 817` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal has not been proceeded with or has been abandoned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 825 the appeal court may order that the appeal be dismissed` MEANS
    IF `there is proof that notice of the appeal has been given` AND (`the appellant has failed to comply with the conditions of a release order made under section 816 or of a recognizance entered into under section 817` OR `the appeal has not been proceeded with or has been abandoned`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on proof that notice of an appeal has been given and that (a) ... or (b) ..."

-- 826 Where an appeal is heard and determined or is abandoned or is dismissed for want of prosecution, the appeal court may make any order with respect to costs that it considers just and reasonable.
