-- 828(2) Where an appeal taken against a conviction or order adjudging payment of a sum of money is dismissed, the summary conviction court that made the conviction or order or a justice for the same territorial division may issue a warrant of committal as if no appeal had been taken.
-- src:17244 | Enforcement by justice
-- src:17245 | (2) Where an appeal taken against a conviction or order adjudging payment of a sum of money is dismissed, the summary conviction court that made the conviction or order or a justice for the same territorial division may issue a warrant of committal as if no appeal had been taken.
@ref Criminal Code s 828(2) (src:17244-17245)
-- @name-test: listed, where/when/upon kind (F-828-2): "Where an appeal taken against a conviction or order adjudging payment of a sum of money is dismissed" answers JUST FALSE
GIVEN `an appeal taken against a conviction or order adjudging payment of a sum of money is dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the summary conviction court that made the conviction or order or a justice for the same territorial division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 828(2) the summary conviction court or a justice may issue a warrant of committal as if no appeal had been taken` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an appeal taken against a conviction or order adjudging payment of a sum of money is dismissed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an appeal taken against a conviction or order adjudging payment of a sum of money is dismissed"
        IF NOT `it is the summary conviction court that made the conviction or order or a justice for the same territorial division` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the summary conviction court that made the conviction or order or a justice for the same territorial division"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 828(3) When a conviction or order that has been made by an appeal court is to be enforced by a justice, the clerk of the appeal court shall send to the justice the conviction or order and all writings relating to that conviction or order, except the notice of intention to appeal and any undertaking, release order or recognizance.
-- src:17246 | Duty of clerk of court
-- src:17247 | (3) When a conviction or order that has been made by an appeal court is to be enforced by a justice, the clerk of the appeal court shall send to the justice the conviction or order and all writings relating to that conviction or order, except the notice of intention to appeal and any undertaking, release order or recognizance.
@ref Criminal Code s 828(3) (src:17246-17247)
DECLARE `s 828(3) document` IS ONE OF
    `s 828(3) the conviction or order`
    `s 828(3) a writing relating to the conviction or order`
    `s 828(3) the notice of intention to appeal`
    `s 828(3) an undertaking`
    `s 828(3) a release order`
    `s 828(3) a recognizance`
    `s 828(3) a document that does not relate to the conviction or order`

@ref Criminal Code s 828(3) (src:17246-17247)
GIVEN `a conviction or order made by an appeal court is to be enforced by a justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      document IS A `s 828(3) document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 828(3) the clerk of the appeal court is required to send the document to the justice` MEANS
    IF `a conviction or order made by an appeal court is to be enforced by a justice`
    THEN CONSIDER document
         WHEN `s 828(3) the conviction or order` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 828(3) a writing relating to the conviction or order` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 828(3) the notice of intention to appeal` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except the notice of intention to appeal"
         WHEN `s 828(3) an undertaking` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except ... any undertaking"
         WHEN `s 828(3) a release order` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except ... release order"
         WHEN `s 828(3) a recognizance` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except ... recognizance"
         WHEN `s 828(3) a document that does not relate to the conviction or order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all writings relating to that conviction or order"
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a conviction or order that has been made by an appeal court is to be enforced by a justice"

DECLARE `s 828 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 828(3) send the conviction or order and the writings relating to it to the justice`

@ref Criminal Code s 828(3) (src:17246-17247)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 828 action`
`s 828(3) the clerk of the appeal court is to send the conviction or order to the justice` MEANS
    PARTY `the clerk of the court`
    MUST `s 828(3) send the conviction or order and the writings relating to it to the justice`
